.TH DV_DEMO 1 "2026-08-21" "diffvim 2.0" "diffvim scripts"
.SH NAME
dv_demo \- 
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dv_demo
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NAME\fR
    dv_demo.sh — Run demo animations for common use cases\fR
\fR
SYNOPSIS\fR
    dv_demo.sh [-h|--help]\fR
\fR
DESCRIPTION\fR
    Runs three pre-configured diffvim animations end-to-end through the\fR
    ad_pipeline driver (compute → postprocess → pace → animator)\fR
    in --no-display mode, so no terminal animator UI is shown — the\fR
    pipeline simply runs to completion and prints progress.\fR
\fR
    The demos exercised are:\fR
      1. Small Python      — tests/tests/examples/01_small_python   (speed 2)\fR
      2. Python Classes    — tests/tests/examples/32_python_classes  (speed 2)\fR
      3. Large Python      — tests/tests/examples/33_large_python    (speed 5)\fR
\fR
    Use this script to smoke-test the pipeline after a build, or as a\fR
    quick "does it work?" check.\fR
\fR
OPTIONS\fR
    -h, --help     Show this help message and exit 0.\fR
                   This script takes no other arguments.\fR
\fR
EXAMPLES\fR
    dv_demo.sh\fR
        Run all three demo animations.\fR
\fR
    dv_demo.sh --help\fR
        Show this help message.\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show detailed help and exit
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR diffvim (1)
